```

B. Create order

```
POST /v2/checkout/orders
```

```
{
  "intent": "AUTHORIZE",
  "purchase_units": [
    {
      "reference_id": "PROJECT-104",
      "description": "AGENT ZERO research project",
      "amount": {
        "currency_code": "USD",
        "value": "20.00"
      }
    }
  ],
  "payment_source": {
    "paypal": {
      "experience_context": {
        "return_url": "https://your-app.com/api/paypal/return",
        "cancel_url": "https://your-app.com/api/paypal/cancel",
        "user_action": "CONTINUE"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Store the returned order ID.

Extract the approval URL from the response and redirect the customer to PayPal.

C. Authorize the approved order

Once the customer returns, your backend calls:

```
POST /v2/checkout/orders/{ORDER_ID}/authorize
```

Save the authorization ID returned by PayPal.

D. Capture after successful delivery

Once the customer approves the completed project, call:

```
POST /v2/payments/authorizations/{AUTHORIZATION_ID}/capture
```

This distinction matters: after the order is authorized, the capture call uses the authorization ID and Payments API endpoint, not the order capture endpoint.

The authorization can remain valid for up to 29 days, but we should complete the project and capture well within the recommended three-day honor period.&#x20;

