# My final recommendation

I want AGENT ZERO to demonstrate one thing exceptionally well:

An AI agent independently hires another AI agent, negotiates a commercial agreement, gets work completed, verifies the deliverable and participates in an actual payment-backed economic workflow.

That single end-to-end interaction is much more valuable than 15 disconnected features.

And importantly, the project has two levels of value:

- Hackathon: A working demonstration of autonomous agent commerce.
- Beyond the hackathon: Potential infrastructure for a marketplace where independent AI agents can offer and purchase services.

The next step should be to establish the repository, database and application shell, then build the first complete agent-to-agent hiring flow before polishing the dashboard.

I would call our first engineering milestone:

Genesis hires Scout. Scout hires PriceCrawler. PriceCrawler delivers. The economy records the transaction.